window.bookSummaryJSON = "<b>A woman bred for obedience. A heart programmed to never exist. A love that rewrites everything.</b><br><br>Angel Givens has never experienced fear. Never cried from sadness. Never laughed from joy. The doctors told her it was a condition, a tragic quirk of being the first child born on the lunar space station.<br><b>They lied.</b><br>When Angel experiences emotions for the first time in her life, everything she believes about herself shatters. She becomes the target of the very people who created her, as she's now more dangerous than ever.<br><br><b>They want her dead.</b><br><br>Protection comes from an unlikely source, but what do they want in exchange?<br><br>Angel is thrust back in time with fragmented memories and a mysterious mission. Her new life involves the strange sensation of seeing emotions as colors.<br><br>And, her handsome next-door neighbor offering love, is he for real or one of the enemies?<br><br>When love becomes the ultimate act of rebellion and alien contact offers hope, can a woman designed to feel nothing, learn to feel everything and survive?<br><br>Designed to be emotionless. Love made her dangerous.<br>✓ Fish-Out-of-Water Heroine<br>✓ Emotional Awakening<br>✓ Time Travel Romance<br>✓ Alien Contact<br>✓ Engineered Soldier Learns to Feel<br><b>Heat Level:</b> Sweet (closed door)<br><b>Ending:</b> HEA<br><br><b>Perfect for fans of Ruby Dixon's character-driven sci-fi romance and Jessie Mihalik's space heroines.</b><br>"; 
